WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.468
-The last time
we talked in this program...

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:04.204
-Yeah.
-It was -- we were talking about

00:00:04.204 --> 00:00:05.271
"Detective Pikachu."
-Yeah.

00:00:05.271 --> 00:00:07.173
-And I said to you, I go,
"Oh, my gosh."

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.875
I go, "Ryan, what's up, man?
What's going on?"

00:00:09.875 --> 00:00:12.645
And you said to me, "Not much."
-Not much, no.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:15.048
-Not much. Yeah, it was great.
We had a fun talk.

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:16.483
Yeah.
-It was really fun.

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.050
And after that, you went
right to the premiere.

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:19.919
-Yep.
-And I get a Google Alert

00:00:19.919 --> 00:00:22.989
saying that Blake is pregnant.
-Oh.

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:25.291
-And...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:28.661
On the red carpet.

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:31.363
-Nobody was more surprised
than me, Jimmy.

00:00:31.363 --> 00:00:32.899
I got to tell you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:35.668
-But I said, "what's up?"
Like, "What's going on

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:37.270
in your life?"
You said, "Not much."

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.805
-I was like, "Not much."
I know.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.272
-Well, kids --
-I thought -- I thought

00:00:40.272 --> 00:00:42.108
the fact that I was wearing
a denim vest

00:00:42.108 --> 00:00:43.710
would be all the rage.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.744
That would be
all over the news.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:46.111
-[ Laughing ]
Gonna be the news there.

00:00:46.111 --> 00:00:48.581
-But then Blake shows up,
uninvited, I might add.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.416
-Oh, my goodness.
That is unbelievable.

00:00:50.416 --> 00:00:52.218
-I thought she's
just been pounding beer.

00:00:52.218 --> 00:00:53.486
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.754
-And it turns out
that she's, like --

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:56.956
She's six months pregnant
or something.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.391
You know?
-Yeah.

00:00:58.391 --> 00:01:00.359
-I got to get way more hands-on
at home.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.727
-You thought -- Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.129
You thought it was gonna be
the denim vest.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:04.363
It wasn't at all.
-No, I thought

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:05.565
that was gonna be
the lead story,

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.099
that that was gonna be
the big Google Alert.

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:08.434
-I will tell you now, 'cause
I thought you were --

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.803
I thought you were trying to--
there was no love for me.

00:01:10.803 --> 00:01:12.671
But I tell you who does have
love for me.

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:14.907
your beautiful daughter James...
-She obsessed with you.

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.843
-...who I love so much.
-My God.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:18.077
-She's the cutest girl.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:20.546
-Jimmy Fallon is Shawn Mendes
to my daughter.

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:23.149
[ Laughter ]
Like, legitimately.

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.550
-She gave me this drawing
last time.

00:01:24.550 --> 00:01:25.685
-She made that drawing.
-And I kept it.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:26.953
Yeah, I hang it in my office.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.387
-She made that drawing
just for you.

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:31.023
When you walk in, though,
she can't even look at you.

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:32.691
She, like, hides in a corner,
and that's it.

00:01:32.691 --> 00:01:34.827
It's hilarious.
-She gets shy?

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:37.063
-Oh, she loses her mind.
-But how does she know me?

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:39.432
-I don't know, Jimmy.
You tell me.

00:01:39.432 --> 00:01:41.567
-I don't know.
I don't know anything.

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.736
-She's up late at night,
watching the damn show.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.272
She's, like, obsessed
with you, though.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:47.574
-But she's --
I love her so much.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.542
James, if you're watching,
go to bed.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.243
-Yes.
-It's almost midnight now.

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:52.611
Go to sleep.
-Yeah.

00:01:52.611 --> 00:01:55.681
-She's actually -- Is she 5?
-She is almost 5, yeah.

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:59.218
-Almost 5. She's so cute.
But I heard that she said to you

00:01:59.218 --> 00:02:02.321
the words that no actor
wants to hear his kid say.

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:04.257
She said she wants
to get into acting?

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:06.826
-She wants to be an actor, yep.
-Oh, my gosh. No, no, no.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:07.960
-And I -- No,
I mean, like, it's --

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.362
I'm fine if she'd want
to be an actor.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:11.497
Like, go ahead.
Like, you know, in school,

00:02:11.497 --> 00:02:14.033
do, like, after-school stuff.
Like, that's all fine.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.402
And right now, it's every day
is, like, a recital.

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:17.636
She's singing songs.

00:02:17.636 --> 00:02:19.439
She's doing little plays
at home, all that stuff.

00:02:19.439 --> 00:02:22.575
But, like, being a child actor
in, like, movies and stuff?

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.911
That's a whole other
ball of wax.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.579
I try to -- I explained to her.
I was like, "Look, you know,

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:28.848
that's a huge burden
on your nervous system.

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:30.083
I mean, having to, you know,

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.685
process all of that attention
and information.

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:34.019
And also you would develop
all of these, like,

00:02:34.019 --> 00:02:36.789
unhealthy coping mechanisms."
And she just looked at me

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:39.158
like she didn't know what the
[bleep] I was talking about.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:40.660
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:42.294
And I was like,
"You know what?

00:02:42.294 --> 00:02:46.065
Here's what's cheaper and easier
is like, let's just skip showbiz

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.966
and enroll you
right into cocaine."

00:02:47.966 --> 00:02:50.402
-No, no, no, no.
That's bad advice.

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:53.139
-Because showbiz
is not good for kids.

00:02:53.139 --> 00:02:54.340
-It's not. No, it's not.

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.509
-I feel like we should
know this by now, right?

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:58.211
-Yes, we should know this.
-But parents everywhere

00:02:58.211 --> 00:03:00.679
are like, "Yeah, let's just put
them in a movie, unsupervised."

00:03:00.679 --> 00:03:01.914
-"Yeah, don't wait.
-"Yeah, it's great.

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:03.282
-I will say, the business can

00:03:03.282 --> 00:03:04.917
get dangerous and edgy because
--

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:07.553
I have an example of something
you recently did.

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.155
You were in Brazil?
-Yeah.

00:03:09.155 --> 00:03:10.723
Oh, yeah, like,
a couple days ago, yeah.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.592
-You got some fans
in Brazil, man.

00:03:12.592 --> 00:03:15.694
Oh, my goodness.
-Yeah, a barricade came down.

00:03:15.694 --> 00:03:17.730
I was kind of buried.
-Was that at Comic Con?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.398
Where was it?
-It was at the Brazil Comic Con.

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:22.268
Yeah, the CCXP Comic Con.
It was an amazing Comic Con.

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.969
But, yeah.
-We actually have a clip.

00:03:23.969 --> 00:03:25.271
Can I just show everyone
what happened?

00:03:25.271 --> 00:03:27.173
Here's the moment
the barricades collapsed.

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.708
Watch this.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.709
[ Crowd cheers ]

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:34.546
I mean, wow.
No one got hurt.

00:03:34.546 --> 00:03:37.049
No one was hurt.
-Oh, man.

00:03:37.049 --> 00:03:39.118
-You jumped up. No one got --
Dude, that was fast reflexes.

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:41.254
-I was not drunk.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:43.790
-You were --
I mean, you jumped backwards.

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.492
-Wow. Yeah, I know.
It felt like slow motion,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:47.994
though, 'cause you see
that they're falling.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.461
You're thinking, "Oh, my God.
Is someone gonna get hurt?"

00:03:49.461 --> 00:03:51.230
And you can see they're all
kind of falling evenly,

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:52.798
like they're gonna go down.
They're gonna be okay.

00:03:52.798 --> 00:03:55.668
And then it was like, "My legs
are not gonna be okay."

00:03:55.668 --> 00:03:57.737
So I jumped back
and landed on the thing.

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.472
-Wow.
-It all happened really fast.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.873
-Is that Steve
from "Stranger Things?"

00:04:00.873 --> 00:04:02.441
-That was Joe Keery from
"Stranger Things,"

00:04:02.441 --> 00:04:04.377
right behind me,
who's in my movie "Free Guy"

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:06.579
that we were there for.
-Did he save you?

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:09.616
-Well, no, if you can see him,
you should look at this back.

00:04:09.616 --> 00:04:11.717
You can see him
saving his beverage.

00:04:11.717 --> 00:04:13.853
He's not worried about --
Watch, watch, watch, watch.

00:04:13.853 --> 00:04:15.688
[ Laughter ]
Yep.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.623
-He just what?
-Out of the way.

00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.292
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:19.292 --> 00:04:20.960
Yeah.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:23.496
He's more concerned about his...
-Yeah.

00:04:23.496 --> 00:04:25.431
That guy's uncomfortable
with the word "hero."

00:04:25.431 --> 00:04:27.600
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:29.235
He was just -- He was
like "The Big Lebowski."

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.170
"I got a beverage, man!"
-Yeah.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:33.238
-Like, getting out of the way,
and, yeah, no.

00:04:33.238 --> 00:04:35.040
-I got to talk to you about it,
because I love

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.642
what you're doing
with your gin.

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:39.211
If you haven't tried
this Aviation gin,

00:04:39.211 --> 00:04:41.314
it is unbelievably
tasty and delicious.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:42.548
-Pretty damn good.
-I do love it.

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.917
It's great, but the ads
and the commercials

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:46.752
that you put on the Internet --
-They're pretty good.

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:47.953
-You know what
I'm talking about.

00:04:47.953 --> 00:04:49.288
They are fantastic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:49.288 --> 00:04:51.424
Every one of them,
a knockout home run.

00:04:51.424 --> 00:04:52.859
Every one, I look forward.
-Thank you.

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:55.160
-But this was
the gift of all gifts.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.564
You got the Peloton girl...
-Yeah.

00:04:58.564 --> 00:05:01.768
-...like, the next day,
to be in your ad.

00:05:01.768 --> 00:05:04.303
-Yeah, within
a few hours of her ad.

00:05:04.303 --> 00:05:06.305
-How did you pull this off,
and why did you do this?

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:08.541
-Well, like, you know,
I've been there

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.976
in that position as an actor,

00:05:09.976 --> 00:05:11.377
where you do something
that doesn't quite work.

00:05:11.377 --> 00:05:13.145
And I really wish somebody
from a gin company

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:14.580
called me right after
"Green Lantern"

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:16.516
and was, like, "Hey."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:20.019
Like, "I got something funny you
can do as an answer to that."

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:22.889
So, yeah,
we got ahold of her.

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:25.124
It was really difficult
'cause nobody wanted --

00:05:25.124 --> 00:05:27.026
nobody knew
how to get ahold of her.

00:05:27.026 --> 00:05:28.460
Obviously, the people at Peloton

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:29.928
didn't want us
to get ahold of her.

00:05:29.928 --> 00:05:32.031
But we got ahold of her,
and within 36 hours,

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:34.867
we had shot and
put out this commercial.

00:05:34.867 --> 00:05:37.403
-What is her name, again?
-Monica Ruiz.

00:05:37.403 --> 00:05:39.805
-Monica Ruiz.
-She's super funny. She's great.

00:05:39.805 --> 00:05:42.040
-I've seen her on talk shows now
because of what you did.

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:43.742
And I hope she gets hired more.

00:05:43.742 --> 00:05:46.145
Monica Ruiz, you are awesome,
and I think she was great.

00:05:46.145 --> 00:05:49.448
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:49.448 --> 00:05:51.784
Let's talk about your movie.
It's on Netflix.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:55.188
"6 Underground" this Friday.
This is the --

00:05:55.188 --> 00:05:56.922
I mean, you guys
know Michael bay.

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:59.625
He does all those giant movies
with a lot of explosions.

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.727
-Yeah, and this was just
one of his home videos.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.262
[ Laughter ]
Home movie.

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.698
-This -- We were talking.
You said, "This is

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:08.101
the Michael Bay-est of
all Michael Bay movies."

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:09.701
-It's the most Michael Bay movie
in the history of Michael Bay.

00:06:09.701 --> 00:06:12.771
-This is the Michael Bay-est
movie ever made.

00:06:12.771 --> 00:06:14.239
-Yeah, the bay-est.

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:17.243
-[ Foreign accent ] This is the
Bay-est I've ever seen.

00:06:17.243 --> 00:06:19.912
-It's absolute Bay-hem.
I could go all day.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:22.514
[ Laughter ]
I could go all day, Fallon.

00:06:22.514 --> 00:06:27.620
-It is -- The first --
I will say, the first 30 seconds

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.556
of the movie,
probably 20 cars explode.

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.658
-Yeah.
-Like nice cars, like Maseratis.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:34.292
-Oh, yeah.
Like, really nice cars.

00:06:34.292 --> 00:06:36.562
-You're racing through Italy,
and it's really Italy.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:38.764
It's not CGI.
-No. No CGI.

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:41.534
We spent a month doing one
car chase in Florence, Italy.

00:06:41.534 --> 00:06:43.836
-That opening car chase
was unbelievable.

00:06:43.836 --> 00:06:45.304
-It's crazy. Yeah.

00:06:45.304 --> 00:06:47.906
-Well, I want to show everyone
just a little taste

00:06:47.906 --> 00:06:50.409
of the car chase you'll see from
the beginning of this movie.

00:06:50.409 --> 00:06:52.478
You'll never see a car chase
like this, ever.

00:06:52.478 --> 00:06:54.046
-Probably not.
-Here's a clip

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.348
from "6 Underground."
Take a look.

00:06:56.348 --> 00:06:58.050
[ Tires screech ]

00:06:58.050 --> 00:06:59.485
-You said,
whatever I need to do, right?

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.520
So I'm just gonna do it.

00:07:01.520 --> 00:07:03.222
-We're definitely gonna be
on the news.

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:05.557
-Hang on.
[ Engine revving ]

00:07:05.557 --> 00:07:07.960
[ Up-tempo music plays ]

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:10.629
[ Tires screeching ]

00:07:10.629 --> 00:07:17.904
♪♪

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:19.405
-No, no, no, no!

00:07:19.405 --> 00:07:21.607
-You were supposed to
have faith.

00:07:21.607 --> 00:07:29.014
♪♪

00:07:29.014 --> 00:07:31.383
-Do you see any choppers?
I don't see any choppers.

00:07:31.383 --> 00:07:34.020
-We lost the chopper.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.587
Not the David.
No, no, not the David.

00:07:35.587 --> 00:07:37.590
Not the David.
Not the...

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.759
-You want to
get out and compare,

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:41.327
or should we maybe
think about going?

00:07:41.327 --> 00:07:43.462
-Nah, I'm good.
-Yep, let's go. Go!

00:07:43.462 --> 00:07:45.998
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Ryan Reynolds, everybody!

00:07:45.998 --> 00:07:49.569
"6 Underground" is available
on Netflix, Friday!

